  "security_implications": "This block gates the debug interface (TL-UL to DMI) based on life‑cycle state, strap sampling, and escalation inputs. Hardened primitives prevent glitch propagation that could spuriously enable debug. The gated TL-UL path returns an all‑zero blank response when disabled, which protects internal data but could mask error information. Integrity errors from both the gate and the adapter are aggregated into a single alert output (intg_error_o). A failure in the latching or the OR-hardened logic could allow unauthorized debug access, undermining life‑cycle security. The separate lc_en signals for the gate and the adapter may introduce a desynchronization risk if the relative timing differs.",
